WEBVTT

00:00:01.980 --> 00:00:05.050
Knowing that our first match is with West Sakuragawa,

00:00:05.050 --> 00:00:09.920
we, the Momoyama Predators, practiced 
very hard, up until the day before the match.

00:00:12.830 --> 00:00:17.230
And now it's the morning of the match.

00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:19.330
Reika-chan, you did it!

00:00:19.330 --> 00:00:20.070
Wow!

00:00:20.070 --> 00:00:21.570
We didn't know if things would work out.

00:00:21.570 --> 00:00:22.900
But thanks to Reika-chan doing her best,{But seeing how hard Reika-chan has been working,}

00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:25.670
we finally feel like we're a team.

00:00:25.670 --> 00:00:28.070
We can definitely win the match today!

00:00:28.070 --> 00:00:30.010
No, we will win!

00:02:10.910 --> 00:02:14.880
Good morning!

00:02:14.880 --> 00:02:17.650
G-Good morning.

00:02:19.950 --> 00:02:22.760
Your voice is too loud as usual, Shou-kun.

00:02:22.760 --> 00:02:24.990
Reika-chan's getting embarrassed.

00:02:24.990 --> 00:02:26.860
What are you saying?

00:02:26.860 --> 00:02:29.600
This pitch is gonna take good care of us today.

00:02:29.600 --> 00:02:31.260
You have to greet it properly!

00:02:31.260 --> 00:02:33.030
I guess so.

00:02:38.970 --> 00:02:42.540
So they are the West Sakuragawa Challengers?

00:02:42.540 --> 00:02:45.380
Yep. They're our first matchup.

00:02:45.380 --> 00:02:48.050
Let's take a look at their skills first.

00:03:01.630 --> 00:03:05.100
Good morning!

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:08.400
What's with that?

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:10.770
They're no good.

00:03:10.770 --> 00:03:13.810
Hey! Stop copying my Kansai accent!

00:03:13.810 --> 00:03:17.110
Eh? Did my accent change?

00:03:17.110 --> 00:03:20.050
Oh well. Just look at them.

00:03:20.050 --> 00:03:23.450
West Sakuragawa was just formed last year.

00:03:23.450 --> 00:03:25.520
They're not worthy opponents at all.

00:03:25.520 --> 00:03:28.090
We can win easily just by kicking the ball around.

00:03:28.090 --> 00:03:29.720
That's no good.

00:03:29.720 --> 00:03:32.420
We have to go all out or else it's disrespectful.

00:03:32.420 --> 00:03:36.460
Well, Shou and Saionji are the 
ones who have to give it their all.

00:03:38.930 --> 00:03:40.330
What are you saying?

00:03:40.330 --> 00:03:44.700
You saw how much Reika-chan has practiced!

00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:45.940
That's right.{Yes, yes.}

00:03:45.940 --> 00:03:50.080
Shou-kun, don't you trip us up during the match.

00:03:50.080 --> 00:03:52.110
Me?

00:03:55.180 --> 00:03:56.980
Don't become a heavy burden.

00:03:56.980 --> 00:03:58.580
O-Okay.

00:03:58.580 --> 00:03:59.890
You're all here so early.

00:04:00.650 --> 00:04:03.020
Good morning, Coach Hanashima.

00:04:03.020 --> 00:04:03.860
Hey.

00:04:03.860 --> 00:04:05.820
You're late.

00:04:05.820 --> 00:04:07.260
What were you doing?

00:04:07.260 --> 00:04:08.960
Oh? Kyouko-san?

00:04:08.960 --> 00:04:11.560
The manager couldn't make it, so I'm here instead.

00:04:11.560 --> 00:04:15.070
Sorry, I was caught up in buying snacks and lunch.

00:04:15.070 --> 00:04:18.470
This is your first match. Do your best!{Do your best during the first match.}

00:04:18.470 --> 00:04:20.840
Come on, stop wasting time.

00:04:20.840 --> 00:04:21.870
Start your warm ups.

00:04:21.870 --> 00:04:23.010
Okay!

00:04:25.840 --> 00:04:27.450
Um, Coach Hanashima.

00:04:27.450 --> 00:04:28.180
Hmm?

00:04:28.180 --> 00:04:30.420
Have you decided on the positions yet?

00:04:36.760 --> 00:04:39.730
I guess so. I'll tell you all when the match begins.

00:04:47.530 --> 00:04:49.540
Mom! Hurry up, hurry up!

00:04:49.540 --> 00:04:52.100
You don't need to hurry that much.{You don't have to be in that much of a hurry.}

00:04:52.100 --> 00:04:53.970
Um, excuse me.

00:04:54.510 --> 00:04:56.810
Is this the way to the People's Exercise Grounds?

00:04:56.810 --> 00:04:57.940
Huh? Y-Yes.

00:04:58.780 --> 00:05:00.410
A guy with weird glasses and a beard!

00:05:00.410 --> 00:05:02.280
H-Hey, Suzu!

00:05:02.280 --> 00:05:03.850
Sorry about that.

00:05:04.980 --> 00:05:06.350
You found out?

00:05:06.350 --> 00:05:12.760
That's right. I'm a guy with 
weird glasses and a beard! Rawr~

00:05:13.660 --> 00:05:15.130
What a weird guy.

00:05:15.130 --> 00:05:17.760
But this is very interesting.

00:05:18.400 --> 00:05:20.170
Look at all the people there.

00:05:20.170 --> 00:05:23.300
The players, their coaches, and 
guardians are all here for different reasons.

00:05:23.300 --> 00:05:25.670
It's quite chaotic.

00:05:25.670 --> 00:05:29.140
Looks like I can get great material today.

00:05:29.140 --> 00:05:30.210
I see.{O-Oh.}

00:05:30.210 --> 00:05:31.510
Well then.

00:05:35.850 --> 00:05:37.420
He really is a weird guy.

00:05:37.420 --> 00:05:38.650
Suzu!

00:05:44.990 --> 00:05:47.460
It's time.{It's finally starting.}

00:05:48.230 --> 00:05:50.960
Coach, the match is about to start.

00:05:50.960 --> 00:05:53.900
Tell us our positions already.

00:05:53.900 --> 00:05:56.440
Well, we already have a good idea of what they are.{Well, we have a good idea of what they are already.}

00:05:56.440 --> 00:05:58.170
Hmm? Really?

00:05:58.170 --> 00:05:59.940
Of course.

00:05:59.940 --> 00:06:02.640
If you take a look at our skills and talents,

00:06:02.640 --> 00:06:04.640
the answer is clear.

00:06:04.640 --> 00:06:08.110
There's a guy who's itching to score goals, right?

00:06:08.110 --> 00:06:09.950
What is it?{What do you want?}

00:06:11.850 --> 00:06:13.520
I see.

00:06:13.520 --> 00:06:18.060
I've decided on your positions today based on your skills and talents.

00:06:18.060 --> 00:06:19.360
Here they are.

00:06:29.370 --> 00:06:32.400
Goalkeeper, Kubota Shunya.

00:06:32.400 --> 00:06:33.340
Okay!

00:06:33.340 --> 00:06:36.540
Left back, Ukishima Yuuto.

00:06:36.540 --> 00:06:37.540
Okay.

00:06:37.540 --> 00:06:40.510
Right back, Saionji Reika.

00:06:40.510 --> 00:06:41.510
O-Okay.

00:06:41.510 --> 00:06:42.510
Do your best.

00:06:42.510 --> 00:06:45.450
Center back, Outa Shou.

00:06:46.120 --> 00:06:48.650
You're the heart of the defense. Do your best.

00:06:48.650 --> 00:06:50.520
O-Okay!

00:06:50.520 --> 00:06:51.560
Yes!

00:06:51.560 --> 00:06:53.730
Onii-chan, go for it!!

00:06:54.190 --> 00:06:56.030
Suzu! Mom!

00:06:56.030 --> 00:06:57.500
Shou!

00:06:58.230 --> 00:07:03.700
My Shou is actually going to play in
 a match! It's like a dream come true!

00:07:03.700 --> 00:07:05.970
Hey, why are you crying!?

00:07:05.970 --> 00:07:07.210
That's going too far.

00:07:07.210 --> 00:07:10.180
Just kidding! Did you fall for it?

00:07:10.180 --> 00:07:11.810
Do your best!

00:07:11.810 --> 00:07:13.010
Mom...

00:07:13.010 --> 00:07:15.110
What a humorous person.{What a jokester.}

00:07:15.110 --> 00:07:16.850
It can't be helped.

00:07:16.850 --> 00:07:20.490
An eternal benchwarmer like
 you is actually playing in a match.

00:07:20.490 --> 00:07:23.320
This may not ever happen again!

00:07:23.320 --> 00:07:24.860
I'm so nervous!

00:07:24.860 --> 00:07:26.460
H-Hey!

00:07:26.460 --> 00:07:28.960
I'm not an eternal benchwarmer!

00:07:28.960 --> 00:07:31.930
I've worked very hard for this day!

00:07:31.930 --> 00:07:35.570
I can see that, but your talent is a bit...

00:07:35.570 --> 00:07:37.740
Let's leave it at that.

00:07:37.740 --> 00:07:40.570
Left half back, Takatou Erika.

00:07:40.570 --> 00:07:43.140
I'm not playing the same position as Ronaldo-sama?

00:07:43.140 --> 00:07:46.910
I want to test these positions for now during the match.

00:07:47.450 --> 00:07:49.780
Right half back, Furuya Ouzou.

00:07:49.780 --> 00:07:51.920
Eh? Two half backs?

00:07:51.920 --> 00:07:54.450
Left midfielder, Tanaka Jun.

00:07:54.450 --> 00:07:55.690
Okay.

00:07:55.690 --> 00:07:58.160
Right midfielder, Uchimura Kei.

00:07:58.160 --> 00:07:58.890
Okay.

00:07:59.390 --> 00:08:01.560
Center midfielder, Furuya...

00:08:02.660 --> 00:08:03.600
Kota.

00:08:03.600 --> 00:08:04.560
Eh?

00:08:05.300 --> 00:08:06.400
What?

00:08:08.370 --> 00:08:11.400
The two forwards will be Uematsu Tarou and Furuya Ryuuji.

00:08:11.400 --> 00:08:12.800
Okay.

00:08:12.800 --> 00:08:14.240
That's all.

00:08:15.140 --> 00:08:16.810
Coach.

00:08:16.810 --> 00:08:17.880
What?

00:08:17.880 --> 00:08:21.610
It seems like you mixed up Kota-kun's and my positions.{It seems like you mixed up my position and Kota-kun's position.}

00:08:21.610 --> 00:08:24.120
No. We'll go with this today.

00:08:24.120 --> 00:08:28.590
You're joking! How can you take Kota away from the forward position?

00:08:28.590 --> 00:08:32.390
Forget about me. Uematsu-kun is a bit weak as a forward.

00:08:32.390 --> 00:08:33.490
Sorry about that.

00:08:35.860 --> 00:08:37.860
H-Hey, everyone.

00:08:37.860 --> 00:08:40.100
Let's do what the coach says.

00:08:40.100 --> 00:08:43.400
Okay? The match is about to start, Kota-kun.

00:08:43.400 --> 00:08:45.100
Let's all form a circle!

00:08:45.570 --> 00:08:47.110
No. I'm fine.

00:08:47.110 --> 00:08:49.110
Us, too.{Me, too.}

00:08:49.110 --> 00:08:50.440
That's that.

00:08:50.440 --> 00:08:52.140
Hey wait!

00:08:52.140 --> 00:08:55.180
I won't say anything during the match.

00:08:55.180 --> 00:08:57.180
Just play however you want.

00:08:57.920 --> 00:09:00.190
However we want?

00:09:00.190 --> 00:09:01.420
Yes.

00:09:01.420 --> 00:09:03.660
It's up to you now, Captain.

00:09:03.660 --> 00:09:05.390
Captain?

00:09:05.390 --> 00:09:07.360
Y-Yes. I'm...

00:09:09.560 --> 00:09:12.830
What should I do? I'm getting all nervous!

00:09:12.830 --> 00:09:15.270
"Can I really be the captain?"

00:09:15.270 --> 00:09:18.740
"I've always been on the bench so far!"

00:09:18.740 --> 00:09:20.540
Don't worry, Captain.

00:09:20.540 --> 00:09:23.240
We've practiced hard for this day.

00:09:23.240 --> 00:09:26.780
We can all play soccer here today thanks to you.

00:09:26.780 --> 00:09:27.810
That's right.

00:09:27.810 --> 00:09:29.650
We're following you, Captain.

00:09:29.650 --> 00:09:30.980
Please, Captain.

00:09:30.980 --> 00:09:33.490
E-Everyone.

00:09:33.490 --> 00:09:35.220
Okay, I get it.

00:09:35.220 --> 00:09:36.990
We'll definitely win the match today!

00:09:37.820 --> 00:09:39.960
Momoyama Predators, fight!

00:09:39.960 --> 00:09:41.860
Fight!

00:09:54.640 --> 00:09:56.580
Let's have a fair match!{Thank you very much! }

00:09:57.580 --> 00:10:01.110
Masaru-chan, you aren't going to give them any orders, right?

00:10:01.110 --> 00:10:03.780
Isn't that a 3-5-2 formation?

00:10:04.380 --> 00:10:07.120
If there's some sort of deep 
meaning behind it, you should tell them.

00:10:09.190 --> 00:10:10.920
This is enough for this match.

00:10:10.920 --> 00:10:12.590
Hmm?

00:10:12.990 --> 00:10:13.890
What's wrong?

00:10:13.890 --> 00:10:15.530
It's nothing.

00:10:15.530 --> 00:10:18.330
I feel that you've changed.

00:10:18.330 --> 00:10:20.000
You were a demonic coach back then.

00:10:20.000 --> 00:10:23.000
You used to give orders right and left.

00:10:23.000 --> 00:10:25.440
They won't mature that way.

00:10:26.070 --> 00:10:29.570
They have to realize something by themselves.

00:10:32.940 --> 00:10:34.150
Heads.

00:10:39.150 --> 00:10:41.820
Did you get any commands from the coach, Captain?

00:10:41.820 --> 00:10:44.220
Nope. He told us to play however we want.

00:10:44.220 --> 00:10:45.720
I see.

00:10:46.260 --> 00:10:49.960
Hey, let's try out Yoi, Big Tri and Build today.

00:10:49.960 --> 00:10:53.170
No, let's forget about that.

00:10:53.170 --> 00:10:55.470
Look at the stands.

00:10:55.470 --> 00:10:57.540
Up above.

00:10:59.170 --> 00:11:01.910
We'll see how good you are today.

00:11:01.910 --> 00:11:03.540
Suguro-kun.

00:11:03.540 --> 00:11:07.310
When we win this match, there's a 
high chance we're playing them next.

00:11:07.310 --> 00:11:09.650
There's no need to show them our tactics.

00:11:10.220 --> 00:11:11.380
I see.

00:11:11.380 --> 00:11:13.420
And about that thing before...{And then there's that messup before.}

00:11:13.420 --> 00:11:15.350
Don't worry about that.

00:11:15.350 --> 00:11:19.160
We're aiming to win like all of you.

00:11:19.160 --> 00:11:21.130
We'll do our best.

00:11:21.130 --> 00:11:22.660
In our own way.

00:11:26.730 --> 00:11:30.070
I'm getting nervous again.

00:11:30.070 --> 00:11:31.740
W-What should I do?

00:11:31.740 --> 00:11:35.510
Is there really anything I can do in this match?

00:11:36.140 --> 00:11:39.140
Misaki-san, I can play soccer again!

00:11:48.820 --> 00:11:52.790
It's okay. I won't be a heavy burden.

00:11:54.760 --> 00:11:56.960
Everyone's nervous.

00:11:56.960 --> 00:11:58.800
Please, Captain!

00:11:59.800 --> 00:12:02.770
That's right. I'm the captain.

00:12:02.770 --> 00:12:05.270
I need to do what I can.

00:12:07.640 --> 00:12:12.240
Everyone! Let's get this started!

00:12:12.240 --> 00:12:14.150
That's too loud!

00:12:19.450 --> 00:12:22.020
I'm finally here.

00:12:22.120 --> 00:12:24.090
Sorry, but it has been decided already.

00:12:24.090 --> 00:12:25.560
Manager!

00:12:27.190 --> 00:12:28.230
You pervert!

00:12:28.230 --> 00:12:28.760
No!

00:12:28.760 --> 00:12:30.660
Please become our coach!

00:12:34.400 --> 00:12:35.800
Isn't that Shou-kun?

00:12:35.800 --> 00:12:38.270
Won't you join our team?

00:12:38.270 --> 00:12:40.440
We are aiming to play the top-flight Rosa.{Our opponents are the top tier team, Rosa.}

00:12:40.440 --> 00:12:41.840
In other words, against adults.{They're adults.}

00:12:43.680 --> 00:12:46.910
Isn't he the drunkard who's always at this park?{Aren't you the drunkard I often see at the park?}

00:12:46.910 --> 00:12:50.150
Best in the country? That goal's too tiny!{Conquer the nation? That's too small of a goal.}

00:12:50.150 --> 00:12:52.450
If you're serious, aim even higher!

00:12:52.450 --> 00:12:54.250
Yes!

00:12:54.250 --> 00:12:56.420
Erika-chan, I have something to ask you.

00:12:59.020 --> 00:13:00.190
The captain's armband!

00:13:00.190 --> 00:13:01.230
Go!

00:13:01.760 --> 00:13:02.690
Okay.

00:13:05.360 --> 00:13:10.070
This is the Momoyama Predators' first match.

00:13:10.070 --> 00:13:12.300
Our kickoff!

00:13:28.720 --> 00:13:29.990
Wow!

00:13:29.990 --> 00:13:32.460
He's putting on that much pressure all by himself.

00:13:32.460 --> 00:13:34.260
What is he thinking?

00:13:34.260 --> 00:13:35.290
If he does that...

00:13:36.590 --> 00:13:38.630
Just kick it forward for now!

00:13:39.930 --> 00:13:40.930
Go!

00:13:40.930 --> 00:13:41.700
Run!

00:13:41.700 --> 00:13:43.870
The ball's coming!

00:13:49.770 --> 00:13:50.480
Wait!

00:14:03.790 --> 00:14:04.690
Over there!{Go!}

00:14:21.840 --> 00:14:23.910
They scored all by themselves.

00:14:23.910 --> 00:14:26.640
Yes! They scored!

00:14:26.640 --> 00:14:30.650
They're amazing! The triplets are so good!

00:14:30.650 --> 00:14:33.450
What's wrong, Masaru-chan? You don't look happy.

00:14:33.450 --> 00:14:35.120
I knew it.

00:14:35.120 --> 00:14:36.860
Good job, Kota-kun.

00:14:36.860 --> 00:14:37.890
Nice shoot!

00:14:36.860 --> 00:14:39.090
Nice goal.

00:14:39.090 --> 00:14:41.560
Hey! How was that nice?

00:14:41.560 --> 00:14:43.830
Oh? Do you have a problem?

00:14:43.830 --> 00:14:47.300
That ball was supposed be mine!

00:14:47.300 --> 00:14:49.000
Why did you steal it from me?

00:14:49.570 --> 00:14:51.840
That's because you were dawdling.{You were being slow.}

00:14:51.840 --> 00:14:53.940
What? You did that on purpose.

00:14:53.940 --> 00:14:56.540
You just wanted to score with only the three of you.

00:14:56.540 --> 00:14:58.640
You did that for your selfish play!

00:14:58.640 --> 00:15:00.040
Selfish play?

00:15:00.040 --> 00:15:01.610
You're mistaken.

00:15:01.610 --> 00:15:05.350
The coach told us to do whatever we want.

00:15:06.320 --> 00:15:08.450
That may be true,

00:15:08.450 --> 00:15:10.820
but you should pass to your teammates more.

00:15:10.820 --> 00:15:14.530
We're only doing what the coach has told us to do.

00:15:14.530 --> 00:15:16.460
If you have a problem, go complain to the coach.

00:15:16.460 --> 00:15:18.400
No way...

00:15:21.400 --> 00:15:28.040
They'll keep the ball amongst themselves until I switch Kota to the forward position.

00:15:28.040 --> 00:15:31.040
But it won't work that easily.

00:15:31.680 --> 00:15:33.810
Man-mark #4, #9, and #10!

00:15:33.810 --> 00:15:34.750
Forget about the others!

00:15:38.780 --> 00:15:40.150
What should I do?

00:15:40.150 --> 00:15:42.390
If this goes on, let alone teamwork...

00:15:43.050 --> 00:15:46.390
...it'll just be Furuyas' game.

00:15:46.930 --> 00:15:50.330
Can't... Can't I do anything?

00:16:04.210 --> 00:16:05.310
Okay!

00:16:08.410 --> 00:16:10.480
No good, no good! Pass it back!

00:16:19.990 --> 00:16:20.890
All right!{Get him! }

00:16:20.890 --> 00:16:21.560
Way to go!

00:16:23.460 --> 00:16:25.330
They're so cute.

00:16:25.330 --> 00:16:26.730
Cute?

00:16:26.730 --> 00:16:30.370
That's right. You're exactly right.

00:16:32.470 --> 00:16:34.840
That's the best way of putting it.{That's the proper expression.}

00:16:34.840 --> 00:16:37.110
You can call this type of soccer cute.

00:16:37.110 --> 00:16:39.440
Oh! The guy with weird glasses and a beard!

00:16:39.440 --> 00:16:40.510
Hey, Suzu!

00:16:42.650 --> 00:16:46.250
But this match is really interesting, and very cute as well.

00:16:46.250 --> 00:16:49.390
In other words, it's very primitive.

00:16:49.390 --> 00:16:52.990
But not exactly so.

00:16:58.430 --> 00:17:00.400
This won't do!

00:17:00.400 --> 00:17:02.830
Everyone other than Reika-chan and me run forward!

00:17:02.830 --> 00:17:04.070
Move the line up!

00:17:04.070 --> 00:17:06.270
You're right. I'll leave defense to you!

00:17:06.270 --> 00:17:07.270
Okay!

00:17:07.270 --> 00:17:12.710
Oh goodness, everyone is running up. 
There are only two people on defense now.

00:17:12.710 --> 00:17:19.350
Well then, young lady. Are they playing the same type of soccer you play in PE class?

00:17:19.350 --> 00:17:22.350
Hmm, it looks a bit different.

00:17:22.350 --> 00:17:25.790
PE soccer didn't have Onii-chan and the others standing in front of the goal.

00:17:25.790 --> 00:17:27.360
It's a huge scramble.

00:17:27.360 --> 00:17:28.860
That's right.

00:17:28.860 --> 00:17:32.830
You can call that primitive soccer. In other words, Dango Soccer.

00:17:32.830 --> 00:17:38.400
What you'll see next is a fierce scramble in front of the goal.

00:17:38.400 --> 00:17:42.270
A huge Dango in front of the goal.

00:17:49.050 --> 00:17:52.480
Yes, yes. The opposing team is trying their best.

00:17:52.480 --> 00:17:53.850
They're so cute.

00:17:53.850 --> 00:17:58.520
They are cute, but this is reality.

00:17:58.520 --> 00:18:02.030
You see this even in professional matches when the two teams differ greatly in skill level.

00:18:02.030 --> 00:18:08.530
In other words, we are analyzing something quite natural.

00:18:11.270 --> 00:18:14.040
Yes, this is beautiful.

00:18:14.040 --> 00:18:18.380
Soccer is all about twenty-two players split into two teams and fighting each other.

00:18:18.380 --> 00:18:20.780
Chaos and drama all rolled up into one.

00:18:20.780 --> 00:18:23.880
That's right! I don't really get what 
you're saying, but it sounds amazing!

00:18:23.880 --> 00:18:26.020
What is he talking about?

00:18:33.890 --> 00:18:35.390
Crap!

00:18:54.080 --> 00:18:56.180
It's a counterattack!

00:18:56.180 --> 00:18:57.380
They're in trouble!

00:18:57.380 --> 00:18:58.880
Aren't you gonna give them commands?

00:18:58.880 --> 00:19:00.890
No, this is fine.

00:19:03.220 --> 00:19:04.690
Reika-chan, please!

00:19:05.620 --> 00:19:07.830
Remember your practice, Reika-chan.

00:19:07.830 --> 00:19:09.260
Block his shooting course!{Prevent him from shooting!}

00:19:27.610 --> 00:19:31.350
What should we do!? They caught up!

00:19:31.350 --> 00:19:32.550
Masaru-chan?

00:19:34.890 --> 00:19:36.220
I'm sorry.

00:19:36.220 --> 00:19:37.920
Don't mind, Reika-chan.

00:19:37.920 --> 00:19:40.590
We're still tied. We're gonna get a lot more goals.

00:19:42.260 --> 00:19:46.000
We kept on pummeling West Sakuragawa after that,

00:19:46.600 --> 00:19:49.970
but the Furuyas never passed to us.

00:19:50.800 --> 00:19:56.810
We had players that were wide open, but the triplets wanted to score themselves.

00:19:56.810 --> 00:20:03.820
Our only other goal in the first half came from Ryuuji-kun luckily hitting one of the opposing players for an own goal.

00:20:13.260 --> 00:20:14.960
Thanks.

00:20:14.960 --> 00:20:16.690
Crap.

00:20:16.690 --> 00:20:20.360
What? That's all Momoyama's got?

00:20:20.360 --> 00:20:23.300
We just have to mark the Furuyas.

00:20:23.300 --> 00:20:25.700
This isn't worth watching. Let's go.

00:20:31.640 --> 00:20:34.650
What's wrong? Is this all you've got?

00:20:35.550 --> 00:20:37.280
Coach.

00:20:37.280 --> 00:20:41.120
Coach Hanashima! Please give us some orders!

00:20:41.120 --> 00:20:44.720
We don't know where to go! Everything's a mess!

00:20:44.720 --> 00:20:47.390
That's your fault.

00:20:47.390 --> 00:20:47.990
Eh?

00:20:47.990 --> 00:20:53.770
No one can match us in skill level.
 That's why we're playing by ourselves.

00:20:53.770 --> 00:20:57.640
Especially you, Saionji. Why were 
you blocking your own goalkeeper?

00:20:57.640 --> 00:21:04.510
Hey! That all started when you angrily kicked
 the ball just because Kota-kun wasn't a forward!

00:21:04.510 --> 00:21:07.010
Who'd want to play that position?

00:21:07.010 --> 00:21:09.580
So you quit because you don't get to play the position you want?

00:21:09.580 --> 00:21:11.020
Are you in kindergarten or something!?

00:21:11.020 --> 00:21:12.150
What did you say?

00:21:12.150 --> 00:21:14.350
Stop that, you two.

00:21:14.350 --> 00:21:16.390
We're a team!

00:21:16.390 --> 00:21:19.820
We can finally play soccer together!

00:21:19.820 --> 00:21:22.030
Now's not the time to fight!

00:21:22.030 --> 00:21:23.390
Shou-kun.

00:21:23.390 --> 00:21:27.430
This is nobody's fault. We need to combine our powers,

00:21:27.430 --> 00:21:29.030
or else we'll lose winning matches!{Or else we'll lose matches we are supposed to win!}

00:21:29.030 --> 00:21:34.640
Forget about being number one in the galaxy. 
We aren't even gonna be number one in Japan!

00:21:38.580 --> 00:21:40.580
Kota-kun!

00:21:40.580 --> 00:21:41.850
Coach Hanashima!

00:21:41.850 --> 00:21:42.950
Please!

00:21:42.950 --> 00:21:44.850
Give us some orders!

00:21:45.680 --> 00:21:47.720
I'm not stepping onto the pitch.

00:21:48.620 --> 00:21:52.390
Who's the one on the pitch that can see everything most clearly?

00:21:57.800 --> 00:21:59.630
That's right.{Is that it?}

00:21:59.630 --> 00:22:02.470
I see what everyone's doing and scream out loud.

00:22:02.470 --> 00:22:05.770
That's the duty of me, the captain!

00:22:05.770 --> 00:22:08.540
Coach, what the hell are you talking about?

00:22:09.240 --> 00:22:12.410
Have you three thought about what you need to do?

00:22:14.250 --> 00:22:16.980
Why haven't we been scoring?

00:22:16.980 --> 00:22:19.820
What should we do about this situation?

00:22:19.820 --> 00:22:21.720
What should I do?

00:22:21.720 --> 00:22:25.060
Think about that yourselves and make your own decisions.

00:22:25.060 --> 00:22:27.790
If the way you're playing is making the match terrible,

00:22:27.790 --> 00:22:30.290
then think about ways of how to make it better.

00:22:31.100 --> 00:22:34.470
You all have to break through this barrier yourselves.

00:22:34.470 --> 00:22:37.170
If you can't, you won't improve.

00:22:37.670 --> 00:22:40.640
We need to think about it ourselves.

00:24:35.550 --> 00:24:36.220
Captain!

00:24:36.220 --> 00:24:38.490
What should we do? The second half's starting!

00:24:38.490 --> 00:24:40.690
The coach told us to think about it ourselves.

00:24:40.690 --> 00:24:43.560
All I can do is let my voice out!

00:24:43.560 --> 00:24:45.430
That's the same as always!

00:24:45.430 --> 00:24:47.500
But I think my feelings will reach everyone.

00:24:47.500 --> 00:24:49.300
That's too much, in more ways than one.

00:24:49.300 --> 00:24:51.440
Everyone's doing whatever!

00:24:51.440 --> 00:24:54.840
Next episode of Ginga e Kickoff! "Breakthrough!"
